#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Ordered contribution-source rules (contains, prefix, or regex); the first match wins. Empty disables normalization."
msgstr "Geordnete Regeln für die Beitragsquelle (contains, prefix oder regex); der erste Treffer gewinnt. Leer deaktiviert die Normalisierung."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Each rule has match, type, and label keys. Regex matches use PHP preg_match syntax including delimiters."
msgstr "Jede Regel hat die Schlüssel match, type und label. Regex-Treffer nutzen die PHP-preg_match-Syntax inklusive Delimitern."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Contribution Source Normalization"
msgstr "Normalisierung der Beitragsquelle"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Telegram Bot API token (from @BotFather)."
msgstr "Telegram-Bot-API-Token (von @BotFather)."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Stored encrypted at rest if Civi key is configured."
msgstr "Wird verschlüsselt gespeichert, sofern ein Civi-Key konfiguriert ist."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Telegram Bot Token"
msgstr "Telegram-Bot-Token"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Fallback chat/group ID used when an action does not specify one. Negative numbers are group chats."
msgstr "Ersatz-Chat-/Gruppen-ID, wenn eine Aktion keine angibt. Negative Zahlen sind Gruppenchats."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Default Telegram Chat ID"
msgstr "Standard-Telegram-Chat-ID"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Fallback URL for the generic Webhook channel when no webhook_url is set on the action."
msgstr "Ersatz-URL für den generischen Webhook-Kanal, wenn an der Aktion kein webhook_url gesetzt ist."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Default Webhook URL"
msgstr "Standard-Webhook-URL"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Bearer token sent as Authorization header. Skip if your webhook uses a different auth scheme — pass it via the action's webhook_headers instead."
msgstr "Bearer-Token, das als Authorization-Header gesendet wird. Entfällt, wenn der Webhook ein anderes Auth-Schema nutzt — dann stattdessen über webhook_headers der Aktion übergeben."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Default Webhook Bearer Token"
msgstr "Standard-Webhook-Bearer-Token"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "ntfy server base URL. Defaults to the public ntfy.sh; set to your self-hosted instance if applicable."
msgstr "Basis-URL des ntfy-Servers. Standard ist das öffentliche ntfy.sh; bei Bedarf auf die selbst gehostete Instanz setzen."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "ntfy Server"
msgstr "ntfy-Server"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Fallback ntfy topic when an action does not set its own."
msgstr "Ersatz-ntfy-Topic, wenn eine Aktion kein eigenes setzt."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Default ntfy Topic"
msgstr "Standard-ntfy-Topic"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Bearer token for protected ntfy topics (Authorization header). Leave empty for public ntfy.sh topics."
msgstr "Bearer-Token für geschützte ntfy-Topics (Authorization-Header). Für öffentliche ntfy.sh-Topics leer lassen."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "ntfy Token"
msgstr "ntfy-Token"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Pushover application/API token (create one at pushover.net/apps)."
msgstr "Pushover-Anwendungs-/API-Token (unter pushover.net/apps anlegen)."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Pushover App Token"
msgstr "Pushover-App-Token"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Default Pushover user or group key. Override per action via pushover_user_key."
msgstr "Standard-Benutzer- oder -Gruppenschlüssel für Pushover. Pro Aktion über pushover_user_key überschreibbar."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Default Pushover User/Group Key"
msgstr "Standard-Pushover-Benutzer-/Gruppenschlüssel"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "From header for the email channel, e.g. \"Herald\" <noreply@example.org>. Leave empty to use the site default from address."
msgstr "From-Header für den E-Mail-Kanal, z. B. \"Herald\" <noreply@example.org>. Leer lassen, um die Standard-Absenderadresse der Site zu verwenden."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Email From Address"
msgstr "E-Mail-Absenderadresse"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Fallback recipient for the email channel when an action does not set email_to."
msgstr "Ersatzempfänger für den E-Mail-Kanal, wenn eine Aktion kein email_to setzt."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Default Email Recipient"
msgstr "Standard-E-Mail-Empfänger"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Topic routing for Herald.publish: map of topic name to delivery params (channel, chat_id, aggregate_minutes, …). A \"default\" entry backs all topics."
msgstr "Topic-Routing für Herald.publish: Zuordnung von Topic-Namen zu Zustellparametern (channel, chat_id, aggregate_minutes, …). Ein Eintrag \"default\" greift für alle Topics."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Topic Routes"
msgstr "Topic-Routen"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Topic the check monitor publishes ok/fail transitions to."
msgstr "Topic, in dem der Check-Monitor ok/fail-Übergänge veröffentlicht."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Monitor Topic"
msgstr "Monitor-Topic"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Internal: last observed status per monitor check (used to detect transitions). Not meant for manual editing."
msgstr "Intern: zuletzt beobachteter Status je Monitor-Check (dient der Erkennung von Übergängen). Nicht für die manuelle Bearbeitung gedacht."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Monitor State (internal)"
msgstr "Monitor-Status (intern)"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Hysteresis: number of consecutive failing runs before a check's fail transition is reported. 1 = report on the first failure (default)."
msgstr "Hysterese: Anzahl aufeinanderfolgender fehlgeschlagener Läufe, bevor der fail-Übergang eines Checks gemeldet wird. 1 = beim ersten Fehler melden (Standard)."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Monitor Open-After Threshold"
msgstr "Monitor-Schwelle zum Öffnen"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Hysteresis: number of consecutive ok runs before a check's recovery is reported. 1 = report on the first recovery (default)."
msgstr "Hysterese: Anzahl aufeinanderfolgender erfolgreicher Läufe, bevor die Erholung eines Checks gemeldet wird. 1 = bei der ersten Erholung melden (Standard)."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Monitor Close-After Threshold"
msgstr "Monitor-Schwelle zum Schließen"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Re-announce a check that has stayed in the reported-fail state this many hours. 0 disables reminders."
msgstr "Einen Check, der so viele Stunden im gemeldeten Fehlerzustand bleibt, erneut melden. 0 deaktiviert Erinnerungen."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Monitor Renotify Hours"
msgstr "Monitor-Erinnerungsintervall (Stunden)"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Map of check-name to ISO datetime: the check produces no fail/renotify alerts until then. Expired entries are pruned on each run."
msgstr "Zuordnung von Check-Name zu ISO-Zeitstempel: Bis dahin erzeugt der Check keine fail- und keine Erinnerungsmeldungen. Abgelaufene Einträge werden bei jedem Lauf entfernt."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "A fail→ok recovery still fires after the snooze lapses if a failure had already been announced before it was set."
msgstr "Eine fail→ok-Erholung wird nach Ablauf der Stummschaltung trotzdem gemeldet, wenn vorher bereits ein Fehler gemeldet wurde."

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "Monitor Snooze"
msgstr "Monitor-Stummschaltung"

#: settings/herald.setting.php
msgid "List of check names that must always be present. A listed check missing from the hook is reported as failing (extension disabled?). Empty keeps the default of silently dropping vanished checks."
